# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mosquitto ACL
#
# Deploy to /etc/mosquitto/acl  (mode 0644, root:root is fine — no secrets)
#
# On :8884 the username is the client certificate CN (use_identity_as_username).
# So `make client CN=gw-01` and `user gw-01` below must agree exactly.
#
# Direction is from the CLIENT's point of view:
#   write = client publishes    (gateway sends uplinks)
#   read  = client subscribes   (gateway receives downlinks)
# Getting these backwards is a common and confusing mistake.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# UG65 topic structure
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The UG65 embedded Network Server does NOT hardcode topics. Under
# Network Server > Application > <app> > MQTT you define one topic per
# Data Type. Available data types (UG65 user guide, Table 3-2-2-5):
#
#   Uplink Data              gateway PUBLISHES device uplinks
#   Downlink Data            gateway SUBSCRIBES for downlink commands
#   Multicast Downlink Data  gateway SUBSCRIBES, multicast group
#   Join Notification        gateway PUBLISHES join accepts
#   ACK Notification         gateway PUBLISHES device ACKs
#   Error Notification       gateway PUBLISHES errors
#   Request data             gateway SUBSCRIBES for NS-API requests
#   Response data            gateway PUBLISHES NS-API responses
#
# `$deveui` in a downlink topic is a wildcard the gateway replaces with the
# real device EUI, letting you address one device — e.g.
#   /milesight/downlink/$deveui
# subscribes to a topic the gateway treats as a per-device pattern. In ACL
# terms that is a single-level MQTT wildcard, so use `+`.
#
# The convention below matches Milesight's own Beaver IoT integration:
#   <prefix>/<gatewayEUI>/{uplink,downlink,request,response}
# (Milesight-IoT/beaver-iot-integrations, MsGwMqttUtil.java)
#
# Substitute your real gateway EUI for 24e124fffef00000 — find it under
# Status > Overview, or on the device label. Then configure the matching
# topics in the gateway UI. Topics are yours to choose; they only have to
# agree on both sides.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Deny everything not explicitly granted below.
# (No global `topic` lines = default deny for authenticated users.)


# --- Gateway gw-01 ---------------------------------------------------------
# CN=gw-01, connects on :8884 with a client certificate.
user gw-01

# Gateway PUBLISHES: uplinks, join/ack/error notifications, NS-API responses.
topic write milesight-gateway/24e124fffef00000/uplink
topic write milesight-gateway/24e124fffef00000/join
topic write milesight-gateway/24e124fffef00000/ack
topic write milesight-gateway/24e124fffef00000/error
topic write milesight-gateway/24e124fffef00000/response

# Gateway SUBSCRIBES: downlink commands. The trailing `+` covers the
# per-device `$deveui` level. Use `/#` instead if you nest deeper.
topic read milesight-gateway/24e124fffef00000/downlink
topic read milesight-gateway/24e124fffef00000/downlink/+
topic read milesight-gateway/24e124fffef00000/multicast

# Gateway SUBSCRIBES: NS-API requests (device provisioning, config).
# Drop this line if you never drive the NS-API over MQTT.
topic read milesight-gateway/24e124fffef00000/request

# Last will — only if you enable Will on the gateway. Topic must match the
# gateway's configured Will Topic exactly.
topic write milesight-gateway/24e124fffef00000/status


# --- Application / backend user -------------------------------------------
# Mirror image of the gateway: reads uplinks, writes downlinks.
# Connects on :8883 with a password (see mosquitto/passwd).
user backend

topic read  milesight-gateway/+/uplink
topic read  milesight-gateway/+/join
topic read  milesight-gateway/+/ack
topic read  milesight-gateway/+/error
topic read  milesight-gateway/+/response
topic read  milesight-gateway/+/status

topic write milesight-gateway/+/downlink
topic write milesight-gateway/+/downlink/+
topic write milesight-gateway/+/multicast
topic write milesight-gateway/+/request


# --- Read-only observer ----------------------------------------------------
# For dashboards. Cannot send downlinks, so it cannot actuate hardware.
user observer
topic read milesight-gateway/#


# --- Debug user (DISABLED) -------------------------------------------------
# Full read/write on every topic, downlinks included, so a cert with CN=debug
# can actuate hardware. Commented out for that reason.
#
# To enable temporarily:
#   1. uncomment the two lines below
#   2. make client CN=debug
#   3. systemctl reload mosquitto
#   4. mosquitto_sub -h <broker> -p 8884 --cafile ca.crt \
#        --cert client.crt --key client.key -t '#' -v
#
# Then REVERT: re-comment, `make revoke CN=debug`, `make crl`, copy the CRL
# across, reload. Revoking matters — re-commenting the ACL alone leaves a
# valid certificate in circulation.
#user debug
#topic readwrite #
